# Cambridge-Ellis School - Git attribute definitions
#
# This repository holds a TypeScript application (Next.js on Vercel, Supabase as
# the data backend) alongside a large committed media corpus. The attributes
# below describe only paths and extensions the repository actually contains.
#
# No Git LFS filter is defined here, deliberately: rendering from committed
# fallback data is a supported runtime state and the one-deploy rollback path,
# so the images under nextjs/public/assets/ must stay ordinary Git objects.

# --- Line endings -----------------------------------------------------------
# Normalize to LF in the repository and check out LF everywhere, so the working
# tree agrees with .editorconfig (end_of_line = lf), with Linux CI and with the
# Vercel build. Anything not declared below is auto-detected from content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Committed binary media -------------------------------------------------
# Declared explicitly rather than left to content heuristics: the deployed asset
# set and the retired archive together hold hundreds of megabytes, and the
# marker also stops diff and merge attempting a textual comparison of a
# multi-megabyte image. `binary` is equivalent to `-text -diff -merge`.
#
# The extension set is measured from the migrated corpus - JPEG, PNG and HEIC
# images plus the PDF, ZIP and DOCX documents whose original URLs are preserved.
# Extensions this repository does not contain are intentionally absent.
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.heic binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.docx binary

# SVG is intentionally NOT binary: app/icon.svg is the sole favicon owner and is
# authored, reviewable XML text.

# --- Generated files --------------------------------------------------------
# Collapsed in review and excluded from language statistics. npm is the single
# package manager, so these are the only two lockfiles in the tree.
nextjs/package-lock.json linguist-generated
tools/package-lock.json linguist-generated

# Migration evidence emitted by the scripts under tools/src: route manifest,
# asset manifest, corpus census, source manifest and parity report. Only those
# JSON reports are generated - artifacts/accessibility-record.md is authored by
# hand each release and is deliberately not matched.
artifacts/*.json linguist-generated

# nextjs/data/fallback/*.json is deliberately NOT marked generated: it is the
# runtime content source in fallback mode and the bounded rollback snapshot, so
# its diffs are reviewed at cutover.

# --- Retired media, staged outside the deployed root ------------------------
# archive/ holds draft-only and unreferenced binaries kept for recoverability,
# including legacy third-party CSS and JS retained as historical artifacts.
# Excluding it keeps retired, non-authored content out of the language
# breakdown. This is the only vendored marker in the tree: the application's own
# stylesheets and configuration are project source and are never marked vendored.
archive/** linguist-vendored
